      "rev_n_8_7786ac_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_7786ac_1",
        "node_id": "n_8_7786ac",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. Thought-2 was indeed the most recent and should be replaced. Here's a better reasoning step:\n\nInstead of attempting to decompose the polyomino into smaller components, we should focus on finding a repeating pattern within the given polyomino. This approach will be more efficient and less likely to produce false positives. We can use a sliding window technique to check for patterns of different sizes, starting from the smallest possible pattern (2x2) up to the full size of the input matrix.",
