        "thought_text": "The current approach is flawed because it only checks for k=2 and doesn't consider all possible base matrices or k values within the input dimensions. This oversight leads to incorrect results and missed solutions. A more effective strategy would be to systematically generate all possible k-powers (2 ≤ k ≤ 5) for all possible base matrices within the input dimensions, ensuring a comprehensive search for a matching solution.",
